/*
 * Bright Star Catalogue, 5th Revised Edition (preliminary), as a packed table.
 *
 * Source:    CDS/VizieR V/50/catalog  (also NASA HEASARC BSC5P)
 * Reference: Hoffleit, D. and Warren, Jr., W.H., 1991, "The Bright Star
 *            Catalogue, 5th Revised Edition (Preliminary Version)".
 *
 * Measured astronomical data, redistributed with the citation above. Not
 * taken from a compiled star database: the widely used HYG merge is CC BY-SA,
 * and a generated table derived from it would be an adapted work carrying
 * ShareAlike obligations into this repository. The underlying catalogue as
 * distributed by CDS and HEASARC carries no such restriction.
 *
 * GENERATED FILE - do not edit. Produced by scripts/gen_star_catalogue.py
 * from the fixed-width source records. The parse was validated against six
 * stars with independently known V and B-V (Sirius, Vega, Betelgeuse,
 * Aldebaran, Capella, Arcturus), and against the true brightness ordering of
 * the six brightest stars.
 *
 * Packing, 6 bytes per star. Worst-case round-trip error across the whole
 * catalogue is 11 arcsec of position, 0.02 in V and 0.01 in B-V - a pixel at
 * 1440p/90deg subtends about 130 arcsec, so position is good to a twelfth of
 * a pixel:
 *   ra    uint16  right ascension, J2000, [0, 65536) over [0, 2pi)
 *   dec   int16   declination,     J2000, [-32767, 32767] over [-pi/2, pi/2]
 *   v     uint8   visual magnitude,       (v / 25) - 2
 *   bv    uint8   B-V colour index,       (bv / 40) - 0.5
 *
 * B-V reaches 5.74 here, which is why its range runs past the 2.5 a naive
 * packing would assume; those stars are real and very red.
 */
